      "text": "Glass is one of humanity's oldest synthetic materials and one of its most transformative. From Egyptian faience to the Venetian monopoly to the float glass revolution to the optical fiber that carries the internet — glass is everywhere and almost invisible. Understanding glass means understanding an unusual material state: ordered enough to be solid, disordered enough to be transparent."
    },
