        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "glassmaking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Overview - Supercooled Liquid: Glass Science and Industry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE GLASS TRANSITION (Tg):\n NOT a phase transition in the thermodynamic sense\n A kinetic phenomenon: at cooling rate typically used,\n  crystal nucleation cannot keep up → liquid \"frozen in\"\n  as disordered solid\n Different from melting point:\n  - Melting: sharp transition, latent heat, entropy jump\n  - Glass transition: gradual; no latent heat; continuous"
    },
