      "text": "The \"glass flows slowly\" myth:\n Cathedral glass is NOT thicker at bottom because it flowed over centuries\n It was manufactured that way — crown glass and cylinder glass had\n non-uniform thickness; glaziers placed thicker end down for stability\n At room temperature, glass is far too viscous to measurably flow\n on any human timescale (would take 10¹⁶+ years for observable flow)\n```"
